{{- /*
  github/shared/pr-working-copy-decision — decide whether the local checkout
  is safe to reuse ("local") for a fix conversation, or whether the child
  must create a fresh worktree ("worktree"). Computed in the babysit parent
  and passed to the spawned fix child so the child never has to guess.

  Callers: babysit-this-pr, babysit-my-prs (§3b Fix CI, §3c/§3d Address
  review comments).

  Placeholders substituted by the agent from the surrounding context:
    <repo path>    — the local checkout of <owner>/<repo>
    <headRefName>  — the PR's branch name

  Outputs (shell variables, consumed later in the spawn payload):
    WORKING_MODE   — "local" or "worktree"
    WORKING_PATH   — the path the child should operate in (or a description
                     of the worktree the child must create)
*/ -}}
Compute the working-copy decision in this parent, then pass it explicitly to
the spawned child — do **not** let the child guess:

```bash
# Are we sitting on the PR branch, clean, and at the PR's head commit?
CUR_BRANCH=$(git -C "<repo path>" rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD 2>/dev/null || echo "")
CUR_HEAD=$(git -C "<repo path>" rev-parse HEAD 2>/dev/null || echo "")
PR_HEAD=$(gh pr view <number> --repo <owner>/<repo> --json headRefOid -q .headRefOid)
DIRTY=$(git -C "<repo path>" status --porcelain 2>/dev/null | head -c 1)
STAGED=$(git -C "<repo path>" diff --cached --name-only 2>/dev/null | head -c 1)

if [ "$CUR_BRANCH" = "<headRefName>" ] && [ "$CUR_HEAD" = "$PR_HEAD" ] \
   && [ -z "$DIRTY" ] && [ -z "$STAGED" ]; then
  WORKING_MODE="local"
  WORKING_PATH="<repo path>"
else
  WORKING_MODE="worktree"
  WORKING_PATH="(child will create a fresh worktree via 'git worktree add')"
fi
```
